{
    /* A lookup table. INPUT holds values in [0, 1); TABLE holds 256 entries
       of any curve — a gamma, a palette channel, a transfer function. Each
       cell of INPUT, scaled to a position, reads the entry there: `I ⌷ X`
       is the cell of X at the position each cell of I names, in X's
       row-major order, and zero where that is no cell of X (a negative
       number, one past the end, NaN). The position is taken by its floor.

       The same read with positions built from the coordinates (`⍳`) is a
       permutation, a resampling or a transpose by hand.

         rhoc examples/lookup.rho
    */
    INPUT:◯ □ 64 64
    TABLE:◯ □ 256

    ((INPUT × 256.0) ⌷ TABLE) → =
}
